    "header_color": "green",
    "pages": [
      {
        "page": 1,
        "total_pages": 2,
        "content": [
          "KIU can join two sentences. It points",
          "back to a noun, a person or a thing,",
          "like WHO, WHICH or THAT in English.",
          "",
          "Jen la foto, kiun mi faris.           Press 1",
          "= Here's the photo (that) I took.",
          "",
          "A COMMA ALWAYS COMES BEFORE KIU, and",
          "after its part if the sentence goes on.",
          "",
          "EACH WORD TAKES ITS OWN CASE:         Press 2",
          "La viro, kiu venis, estas mia frato.",
          "= The man who came is my brother.",
          "La viro, kiun mi vidis, estas mia frato.",
          "= The man (whom) I saw is my brother.",
          "KIUN is the object of VIDIS: it takes -n.",
          "LA VIRO is the subject of ESTAS: no -n."
        ],
        "pronunciation": "Leciono dudek kvin",
        "pronunciation_mappings": {
          "1": "Jen la foto, kiun mi faris.",
          "2": "La viro, kiu venis, estas mia frato. La viro, kiun mi vidis, estas mia frato."
        }
      },
      {
        "page": 2,
        "total_pages": 2,
        "content": [
